# Raw + processed data: 150MB, regenerated in ~1 min by `python run.py data`.
# The dataset is fetched from the Hugging Face Hub, so there is no reason to
# vendor it -- but a small labelled sample IS committed so the repo demos
# without a download.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
# The 1% demo slice IS committed (2.5MB): without it a fresh clone has nothing
# to score, and the dashboard's Live Score tab is the first thing anyone opens.
!data/processed/demo.parquet

# Model artefacts (~1.1MB) and reports (~700KB) ARE committed on purpose:
# they are the evidence a reviewer reads, and they let a fresh clone start the
# API and the UI without first sitting through a 20-minute Optuna run.
# Only the two regenerable, noisy artefacts are excluded:
reports/audit_log.jsonl
reports/review_queue.jsonl
reports/hold_queue.jsonl
reports/optuna.db
reports/*.log
reports/*_log.txt

# Validation predictions are per-run training checkpoints (17MB). They make a
# retrain resumable but are not needed to serve, and they go stale the moment
# a model is refitted.
models/val_preds/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env
logs/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
